silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_03_probe_domesticcat_collapse_yoneda_hom_leg_2 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ProbeDomesticCatCollapseLegLambdaClsExample" .
silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_03_probe_domesticcat_collapse_yoneda_hom_leg_2 silm:hasExample "In 'ProbeDomesticCatCollapseLegLambdaCls', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §11.1: A diagram D: J -> A in a category specifies which nodes are distinct objects. Here the classification leg lambda_cls: Mittens -> DomesticCat exits the apex outward into the classification sort, while the taxonomy identification arrow iota_tsn enters the apex from TaxRow_TSN183798. The two arrows live in disjoint hom-sets Hom(Mittens, DomesticCat) and Hom(TaxRow, Mittens) which cannot be identified without collapsing the cocone to a loop. This separation is the probe-R3 invariant." .
